items: bugs-index-selftest-fails-on-a-shallow-clone
paths: file:tests/e2e/bugs-index-gate.sh
scope: |
  main is RED on every push and has been for an hour. The new stale-open report is guarded with
  `not SHALLOW` -- correct, it needs `merge-base --is-ancestor` -- but the SELF-TEST asserts the
  report fires unconditionally. CI checks out with actions/checkout@v4 and no fetch-depth, i.e.
  SHALLOW, so the assertion can never hold there. Not mine; my commits are just the pushes that ran
  it. Reproduced in a `git clone --depth 1`, which is the control this needs.
next: make the assertion conditional on the same SHALLOW the check uses, and prove it in both clones
